From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] framework: the light themes' chrome colour is white

Measured on V86 (2026-10-27) from raw framebuffer grabs, by region rather
than over whole pages:

  PackageInstaller, the header band of every install screen  grey 245, 1072 x 95 px
  Settings sub-page title bar (storage, about, apps, ...)    grey 245, about 106,000 px
  Settings storage page, the band under the title bar        grey 238, 239,300 px

Rule 1 of docs/design/eink-ui.md: #F5F5F5 and #EEEEEE land on the panel's
14th level, which is not told apart from white, so they may not be used to
separate one region from another. Three colours put them there, and all three
are pass-throughs whose only readers are a theme's colorPrimary or
colorSecondary:

  primary_material_light           colorPrimary of Theme.Material.Light, and
                                   through colors_device_defaults.xml of
                                   Theme.DeviceDefault.Light -- the action bar
                                   (Widget.Material.ActionBar) and the ten
                                   ?android:attr/colorPrimary backgrounds in
                                   PackageInstaller's install and uninstall
                                   layouts
  primary_material_settings_light  colorPrimary of Theme.Material.Settings.Light
                                   and Theme.DeviceDefault.Settings.Light
  secondary_material_settings_light  colorSecondary of the same two

So one value each, at the point where the chrome colour is named, rather than
one patch for every application that reads it. The greys themselves
(material_grey_100, material_grey_200) are a palette and are left alone.

colorEdgeEffect is ?attr/colorPrimary as well, so the overscroll glow turns
white with the rest: rule 5 asks for no gradients, and a glow that is drawn in
two or three 134 ms frames is the kind this device cannot afford. Nothing else
in core/res reads these three names.

Where a bar still needs an edge, the edge is black and drawn by the
application: patches/aosp-settings/0008 gives the Settings action bar and the
storage band a 2 px black rule under a white ground (rule 3). This patch is
what makes every other light-theme bar white.

Only values change. No name is added, and nothing is written above an entry:
com.android.internal.R, framework.jar and the 45 ART boot files stay as they
are. Patch 0060's header records what happens when a comment is put above an
entry in this file.

--- a/core/res/res/values/colors_material.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/colors_material.xml
@@ -26,9 +26,9 @@
     <color name="background_floating_material_light">@color/white</color>
 
     <color name="primary_material_dark">@color/material_grey_900</color>
-    <color name="primary_material_light">@color/material_grey_100</color>
+    <color name="primary_material_light">@color/white</color>
     <color name="primary_material_settings">@color/material_blue_grey_900</color>
-    <color name="primary_material_settings_light">@color/material_grey_100</color>
+    <color name="primary_material_settings_light">@color/white</color>
     <color name="primary_dark_material_dark">@color/black</color>
     <color name="primary_dark_material_light">@color/material_grey_600</color>
     <color name="primary_dark_material_light_light_status_bar">@color/material_grey_300</color>
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@
     <color name="primary_dark_material_settings_light">@color/material_grey_300</color>
 
     <color name="secondary_material_settings">@color/material_blue_grey_800</color>
-    <color name="secondary_material_settings_light">@color/material_grey_200</color>
+    <color name="secondary_material_settings_light">@color/white</color>
     <color name="tertiary_material_settings">@color/material_blue_grey_700</color>
     <color name="quaternary_material_settings">@color/material_blue_grey_200</color>
 
